ng("0x0005a48a", "injection_timing_top_dead_center_offset", "i16",
   "Code: three users, all word loads (lha = signed; xref_addr.py: 4 reads / 0 writes, 3 functions, ROM, no boot-ROM user): (1) cm848_j1939HandlePgn65504ProprietaryB sends ((main_injection_timing + this) x 120 >> 10) + 125, i.e. main timing relative to top dead center in degrees (120 / 1024 = 0.1171875) with the J1939 offset; (2) cm848_calculateAuxiliaryInjectionTiming sets auxiliary_injection_timing = -(this + retard) when injection_timing_auxiliary_top_dead_center_referenced_flag is set, i.e. retard counts after top dead center; (3) cm848_calculateMainInjectionTiming adds it in injection delivery mode 3 (timing = demand + injection_timing_offset_cal + this, clamped +-1024). ROM value -171 counts = -20.04 deg (neighbour 0x5a488 = -253). Uses (1) and (2) agree that counts = degrees-from-top-dead-center + 171, so the constant is the (negative) top dead center position in timing counts. SIGN OF USE (3) NOT SETTLED: it adds the same -171 to a demand in delivery mode 3, which is the opposite of the conversion in (1) and (2) unless that demand is already top-dead-center relative in the other direction. Medium confidence; the name only says 'offset', not the sign.")
